            <td>3.9 times faster</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>The I/O, HBM3E, and rack figures come from Engineering at Meta, 24 August 2026. The production status comes from Meta's news post of 11 March 2026, which also says hundreds of thousands of MTIA chips are already deployed for inference across organic content and ads. Organic content means regular posts rather than ads. I/O is how fast data moves in and out of the chip. RDMA NICs are network cards that let chips read each other's memory directly. Scale-up links chips inside a rack, and scale-out links racks to each other. GEMMs are the large matrix multiplications at the heart of AI math, and collectives are the group data transfers between chips.</p>

    <h2 class="ai-model-section">MTIA 400</h2>
    <p>The 300 evolved into the 400 to support GenAI models while keeping the ranking and recommendation workloads. GenAI, or generative AI, means models that write text or make images. Lab testing of the 400 is finished. On 11 March 2026 Meta said the 400, 450, and 500 will handle all workloads, and will be used mainly for GenAI inference in production in the near future and into 2027.</p>
