    <h2 class="ai-model-section">2nm accelerator</h2>
    <p>Broadcom's 14 April 2026 release calls the part the industry's first 2nm AI compute accelerator and says the technology supports MTIA. 2nm names the chip manufacturing process, and a smaller number means a newer, denser process. The gigawatt commitment and the 2029 term are on the <a href="/ai/hardware/chips/meta/">Meta stack</a>.</p>

